      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:47:4",
      "text": [
        " الصَّبْرُ مِنَ الْإِيمَانِ بِمَنْزِلَةِ الرَّأْسِ مِنَ الْجَسَدِ وَ لَا إِيمَانَ لِمَنْ لَا صَبْرَ لَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Ali Bin Al Hakam, from Abu Muhammad Abdullah Al Sarraj, ",
          "(It has been narrated) raising it to Ali<sup>asws</sup> Bin Al-Husayn<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The patience from the <span class=\"iTxt\">Emān</span> is at the status of the head to the body, and there is no <span class=\"iTxt\">Emān</span> for the one who has no patience for him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Ali ibn al-Hakam from abu Muhammad ‘Abd Allah al-Sarraj who has narrated in a marfu’ manner from Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.) who has said the following: “Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.) has said, ‘Patience is to belief as the head is to the body. One who does not have patience has no belief.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
